{"id": "swebq0186", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That depends on what you're interested in. If you want to learn about the history of the universe and science, I would recommend reading \"A Brief History of Time.\" It's a classic that explains complex ideas like black holes and the Big Bang in an accessible way. But if you' re more interested in how the human mind works, then check out \"The Bi ology of Belief\" or even his earlier book \"The Selfish Gene.\" Both are great entry points depending on your curiosity.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
